EctoPad SunPad-native iOS menu correction, 2026-08-13

Keep SunPad's actual `UIButton.menu` / `UIMenu` implementation instead of an
EctoPad-specific `UIAlertController` action-sheet fallback.

- `showsMenuAsPrimaryAction = YES`;
- Render Resolution, Aspect Ratio, and Game Data & Saves remain native nested
  `UIMenu` children;
- UIKit owns submenu navigation and outside-tap dismissal;
- keep SunPad's icons, selection-state checks, haptics, and refresh behavior;
- only product strings change from SunPad to EctoPad;
- render/aspect actions additionally notify EctoPad's renderer bridge after
  persisting the shared setting.

The removed fallback was physically rejected: it rendered as an oversized
action sheet, nested actions did not present, and tapping outside did not
dismiss it. Do not reintroduce a parallel custom menu surface.

Physical follow-up then showed that the restored `UIButton.menu` still did not
open while the overlay was attached directly to the SDL `UIWindow`. SunPad
owns the overlay from its active game view controller. EctoPad now mirrors
that hierarchy by adding the unchanged overlay to
`window.rootViewController.view`, keeping the FPS label in the same host, and
reasserting z-order within that controller-owned view. A bounded
`UIControlEventTouchDown` diagnostic records whether the physical tap reaches
the menu button and names its host/controller.

Physical testing then accepted the native menu actions: Render Resolution,
Aspect Ratio, and FPS all changed live. The separate game main menu remained
difficult to read, so its dynamic option panes now explicitly use white text
with black outlines. Hardware rejected that first attempt because
`CGuiTextPane::Draw()` replaced the geometry color every frame. The current
build marks only these menu labels for a render-time white geometry override
and makes unselected table entries 90% white/fully opaque.

The supplied screen was then identified as `FRME_NewFileSelect`, not the
separate `SFrontEndFrame`. Recoloring both panes created bright duplicate text;
recoloring only pane A left pane B as a black duplicate. All render-level text
overrides were removed. The final compatibility correction suppresses pane B's
offset pass only in this frame. Pane A keeps the original game strings,
typewriter animation, widget geometry, and table-selected/unselected colors.
The exact implementation is `UseSingleReadableFileMenuPane`: set pane A's
font color to white and call `SetIsVisible(false)` on pane B for the file rows,
root choices, and popup choices in `FRME_NewFileSelect`. The user physically
accepted this solution on 2026-08-13. Do not replace it with a global geometry
color override or recolor both authored panes.

The UIKit `•••` button is non-focusable, disables pointer focus, and provides
the ellipsis image for selected and selected+highlighted states to prevent the
brief empty/square focus artifact after native menu dismissal.

Foreground recovery now observes UIKit lifecycle notifications and reattaches
the existing overlay to the current SDL root-controller view when its host was
replaced. Periodic recovery performs the same host check. Diagnostics persist
the lifecycle name, old/new host, window attachment, menu attachment, and touch
visibility.
